<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-AWB Australian wheat indicator prices - Feb 11.</title>
<headline>RTRS-AWB Australian wheat indicator prices - Feb 11.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian Wheat Board international card prices for wheat exports for Feb 11.</p>
<p>In U.S. dollars per tonne, FOB eastern states.</p>
<p>		ASW	  AH     PH 13 PCT  PH 14 PCT</p>
<p>    Feb    200.00    204.50    207.00     218.00</p>
<p>    Mar    200.00    204.50    207.00     218.00</p>
<p>    Apr    199.00    203.50    206.00     218.00</p>
<p>    May    199.00    203.50    206.00     218.00</p>
<p>    Jun    199.00    203.50    206.00     218.00</p>
<p>    Jul    197.50    202.00    204.50     216.50</p>
<p>Note: ASW = Australian Standard White; AH = Australian Hard; PH = Australian Prime Hard; percentages = protein content.</p>
<p>Australian Wheat Board indicator prices for multi-grade contracts for 1997/98 crop wheat increased by A$3.00 a tonne.</p>
<p>	  Indicator Prices in A$ per tonne:</p>
<p>		  ASW 10 pct protein</p>
<p>National FOB	168.00</p>
<p>Indicator prices on a delivered port basis:</p>
<p>    Queensland			   South Australia</p>
<p>    Mackay	  143.50	    Port Adelaide	 145.00</p>
<p>    Gladstone     143.75	    Port Giles	    145.75</p>
<p>    Brisbane	141.50	    Wallaroo		143.50</p>
<p>    New South Wales</p>
<p>    Pt Pirie	140.50</p>
<p>    Newcastle     143.50	    Pt Lincoln	    146.75</p>
<p>    Port Kembla   144.00	    Thevenard	     141.75</p>
<p>    Victoria			     Western Australia</p>
<p>    Geelong	 143.00	     Esperance	    148.25</p>
<p>    Portland	144.00	     Albany		 149.25</p>
<p>					     Fremantle	    151.25</p>
<p>					     Geraldton	    149.25</p>
<p>NOTE: The indicator price represents the current state of the international wheat market. It is a cash contract price quoted on a delivered port basis, offered today by the AWB for wheat delivered during the 1997/98 harvest. The offer is valid until 4.30 p.m. Australian Eastern Standard Summer Time (0530 GMT).</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
